## Your Task

- **ID**: TASK-260715-2ny6z4
- **Title**: Record the SSH transport conformance contract
- **Parent**: STORY-260715-lkshfz
### Description

Translate the SSH transport specification into a candidate-neutral implementation and test contract for connection, host verification, authentication, direct-tcpip, exec, windows, rekey, backpressure, cancellation, metrics, and lifecycle.
### Scope

In scope: Swift async interface and state ownership; raw host-key evidence before acceptance; supported auth outcomes; destination and originator endpoints; byte-channel and exec semantics; bounded write contract; half-close; per-channel receive windows and adjustment; client byte and time rekey; server rekey; keepalive; cancellation; error taxonomy; metric schema; lane identity for experiments; dependency injection. Out of scope: choosing a candidate, production lane scheduling, flow migration, SFTP, ProxyJump, interactive UI, relay framing, and final window constants.
### Acceptance Criteria

1. A TASK-ID-scoped contract defines every operation, state transition, cancellation point, timeout, ownership boundary, error, metric, and privacy rule required by the M0 matrix. 2. Host-key bytes, algorithm, and fingerprint evidence are available to policy before authentication acceptance, including first-use, match, and change cases. 3. Direct-tcpip and exec channels have explicit open, bounded write, read, EOF, half-close, reset, cancel, and close semantics. 4. Window policy, WINDOW_ADJUST, automatic byte and time rekey, explicit test trigger, server rekey, keepalive, and key-exchange channel behavior are independently observable. 5. The conformance contract can be implemented by either candidate without exposing candidate types to ReluxTunnelCore consumers.

## Instructions

The following instructions have been attached to this task:

### TASK-260715-2ny6z4_inputs.md
> SSH conformance contract inputs

Record the SSHTransport CONFORMANCE contract that BOTH engine adapters (ReluxNIOSSH fork via TASK-260715-nzdzv3; libssh2 via 1af33i/1ozsb6) must satisfy so they are interchangeable behind the ReluxTunnelCore SSHTransport boundary (TASK-260715-2nfz7w). INPUTS: TASK-260715-28ok1k audit — SwiftNIO SSH has NO public per-channel window setter/observer (16 MiB internal target) and _rekey() is internal (fork must expose both); libssh2 exposes per-channel windows publicly (channel_open_ex / window_read_ex / receive_window_adjust2) but has NO client-initiated rekey threshold (adapter must schedule rekey manually); NIOSSH has no RSA host keys, libssh2 has RSA-SHA2. .spec/ssh-transport.md, ADR-005 (direct-tcpip + exec), ADR-006 (exec-stdin upload, NO SFTP), ADR-014 (selection OPEN). DELIVER the conformance contract: connect + MANDATORY host-key verification before user auth (ed25519/ecdsa/rsa fingerprint + changed-key stop policy per security-privacy.md); openDirectTCPIP; openExecChannel; upload via exec-stdin; PER-CHANNEL WINDOW interface (settable initial window, observable remaining, explicit cap — required of BOTH adapters; matches audit E-WINDOW); REKEY interface (client-initiated by byte/time threshold — required of BOTH); keepalive; channel close/cancel/error semantics; concurrency expectation (hundreds..1000 channels). Define the conformance TEST MATRIX both adapters run (audit E-ALGO/E-HOSTAUTH/E-CHANNELS/E-SCALE/E-WINDOW/E-REKEY) so TASK-260715-2d3g5e implements ONE suite against BOTH. Keep the engine INJECTABLE; do NOT select it (that is 1gjxer). Contract doc only.




